{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1093756-trolls-and-oaths","id":1093756,"title":"Trolls and Oaths","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-17T12:48:20-07:00","id":1093756,"title":"Trolls and Oaths","content":"A couple questions about trolls and oaths. First, let's assume there are a few troll characters that greatly fancy the nomad lifestyle (perhaps they have more than a little eshu in their natures) and as a result they really don't want to be tied down by swearing any oaths of guardianship, loyalty, protection, love, or friendship to local nobles or groups, fixed things, or people that don't share their lifestyle. Yet, they do wish to have some oaths, because their natures do drive them to that to feel fulfilled, and because they don't want to be perpetually locked out of their Birthright. Short of the loophole of swearing some kind of bond with their traveling companions, what kind of oaths might be appropriate for this kind of characters to have? They want to be honorable, they just don't want to be tied down to anyone (except possibly soulmates sharing the endless road) or anything. Second, and quite possibly relevant to the former issue: if a troll does join a House, and swears loyalty to its ideals, does this oath count for Birthright purposes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:52:49-07:00","id":1093757,"title":"","content":"It's more than just honour, they generally want purpose. So some sort of oath to fulfill that purpose would make sense. <br /> <br /> And yes, I'm pretty sure (I'm not a developer and I don't have an explicit cite though) that the oath when you join a house counts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T12:55:14-07:00","id":1093758,"title":"","content":"An Oath swearing to uphold a code of conduct or refrain from certain activities would be apropos. An Oath to a chimerical companion. An Oath to seek something, learn something, or undergo some experience. The Oaths in Chapter 6 are just sample Oaths. <br /> <br /> And yes, a House Oath counts for Birthright purposes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T13:03:27-07:00","id":1093767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1093756-trolls-and-oaths?p=1093757#post1093757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's more than just honour, they generally want purpose. So some sort of oath to fulfill that purpose would make sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Purpose is fine. I'm just trying to puzzling out what kind of oath would be appropriate for them to find it by being the Knight Errant or Wandering Heroine rather than the Guardian/Enforcer of (X) and avoid being potentially bolted down to the same locale for an entire chronicle in order to fulfill an oath.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, I'm pretty sure (I'm not a developer and I don't have an explicit cite though) that the oath when you join a house counts. </div> </div> </div>That would be nice.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T13:10:50-07:00","id":1093772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gl1tterboots</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1093756-trolls-and-oaths?p=1093758#post1093758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An Oath swearing to uphold a code of conduct or refrain from certain activities would be apropos. An Oath to a chimerical companion. An Oath to seek something, learn something, or undergo some experience. The Oaths in Chapter 6 are just sample Oaths.</div> </div> </div> </div>These seem good ideas. About the latter part of your examples, the 'quest' oaths, let's assume the character does fulfill one after a while, so the oath expires successfuly. Does it still count for Birthright purposes, or does the character have to swear a new one to keep their power? If the latter, does the character have some kind of grace period? Of course, since the Dreaming does not allow itself to be cheated, I'm assuming the character does not attempt to abuse their Birthright by swearing to do trivial quests.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 05-17-2017, 04:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T17:06:47-07:00","id":1093901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1093756-trolls-and-oaths?p=1093767#post1093767\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Purpose is fine. I'm just trying to puzzling out what kind of oath would be appropriate for them to find it by being the Knight Errant or Wandering Heroine rather than the Guardian/Enforcer of (X) and avoid being potentially bolted down to the same locale for an entire chronicle in order to fulfill an oath.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;I swear to travel the Autumn world and Fight evil wherever I might Find it. I swear to never claim a home but the open road.&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> There's also a bunch of kngihtly orders for your Knights Errant to join, Cold watch, Red Branch etc<br /> <br /> <br /> If the character's purpose is to be a wandering champion who comes in cleans up the town and rides off build oaths around that. And there's always the easy one of Oathcircle with the fellow pcs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T07:13:03-07:00","id":1094112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1093756-trolls-and-oaths?p=1093772#post1093772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> These seem good ideas. About the latter part of your examples, the 'quest' oaths, let's assume the character does fulfill one after a while, so the oath expires successfuly. Does it still count for Birthright purposes, or does the character have to swear a new one to keep their power? If the latter, does the character have some kind of grace period? Of course, since the Dreaming does not allow itself to be cheated, I'm assuming the character does not attempt to abuse their Birthright by swearing to do trivial quests.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think it makes for a good character arc to have a Troll complete an Oath, feel their strength fade, and when they make a new Oath feel reinvigorated and empowered by the Dreaming. As for making trivial Oaths that borderline exploit their strength, that sounds entirely like an Unseelie troll's prerogative <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13420-gl1tterboots","name":"gl1tterboots","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T07:19:09-07:00","id":1094114,"title":"","content":"Also, those kind of oaths seem like something the Dreaming would come up with situations to make a lot more challenging than you might think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T13:19:02-07:00","id":1095600,"title":"","content":"The most obvious open-ended oaths that I can think of would be along the lines of &quot;His enemies will never have his sacred ring!&quot; and &quot;Your secret dies with me.&quot;<br /> <br /> Both are aided by moving around so that interested enemies can't find you, whether to pry the ring from your fingers or the secret from your lips.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-22T14:24:06-07:00","id":1095618,"title":"","content":"I swear to wander wherever the Path, the Sun, and the Moon should take me and never to settle until I stand once more before the Gates of Arcadia, where I can finally rest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1383-yrtalien","name":"yrtalien","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"97"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-13T18:01:18-07:00","id":1115739,"title":"","content":"Yes, I'm dredging up an old thread as I explore the forum. But this one spoke to me because I strongly identify as a troll IRL. <br /> <br /> Trolls do not have to make oaths! There is nothing in their birthrights or frailty that says they must have an active oath at any given time. This is also not stated in KB:Troll. In fact, it's explicitly stated that trolls are very careful about the oaths they make since they are more bound to them than any other kith. A troll may be one of the <i>least</i> likely to swear an oath, depending on the situation, because they know if they break it the Dreaming will come down on them harder than anyone else. So in the original premise I would first ask &quot;<i>Why</i> is the troll swearing any sort of oath?&quot; If he/she doesn't have to for a darn good reason, then they shouldn't. It's perfectly acceptable for a troll to have no outstanding oaths at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T02:29:53-07:00","id":1127987,"title":"","content":"Yes, this may be the thread that won't stay down. Appropriate for the topic.<br /> <br /> You make an interesting point about trolls without oaths. I was just re-reading the kith description and I realised that from that perspective, the troll quote can be seen as a short-term oath.<br /> <br /> \u201cDraw your blade. Call your friends. Bring ax, sword, bullets. I\u2019m not moving.\u201d<br /> <br /> In other words, the troll swears that, in this situation, it's not going to be him who backs down. It also makes coming back later the smart choice for his opponent since the troll won't be oathbound if they take him by surprise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13395-daniel-knight","name":"Daniel Knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-12T19:13:21-07:00","id":1128301,"title":"","content":"And remember that a troll can be quite stubborn and strong-willed without officially swearing an oath. In that quote there is nothing that is framed as a true oath. It's just the troll standing their ground and making their viewpoint known. Because they are a troll they will be unlikely to back down from the statement even though it's not an official oath. But if they did, they wouldn't suffer any ill effects. In C:tD an oath is backed by the power of the Dreaming. It's more than just a promise, it's a binding contract with the Dreaming as the &quot;lawyer&quot; overseeing the deal. &quot;I'll come back for you&quot; may be a promise of sorts but it's not the same as &quot;By the power of the Dreaming and with all of my essence I vow to return to you no matter the dangers or circumstances&quot;. A troll stating the former would lose nothing (other than maybe personal honor) if they didn't come back, but a troll stating the latter would have their frailty hit them with full effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://imgbb.com/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://image.ibb.co/fzeOgQ/1172c70f3ff188688852c74c8145285c_original_2_4.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> Visit my freehold for Changeling links, settings, art, and other goodies.<br /> <a href=\"https://theshepherdsfreehold.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The Shepherd's Freehold</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13648-shepherd","name":"Shepherd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}